{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/486446-streamlining-combat","id":486446,"title":"Streamlining combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-20T09:12:03-07:00","id":486446,"title":"Streamlining combat?","content":"For me, combat resolution mechanics are something that tends to get in the way of a good story, and de-rail mood and pacing into laughing at bad rolls. I fully understand why people like combat-heavy settings and games, they are just not what I want to ST.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, combat is both interesting and useful as a storytelling tool. And I do like to describe in detail the plasm-filled aftermath of a Spectre's claw attacks.<br /> <br /> Still, I'd quite like to streamline how combat works in Wraith. Currently, a single combat action requires the following rolls (and potential shadow dice):<br /> 1, Initiative<br /> 2, Attack<br /> 3, Dodge<br /> 4, Deal damage<br /> 5, Soak damage.<br /> +armour, complications, special melee moves, etc, etc that can mess with the flow<br /> <br /> That is a _lot_ of rolling (twenty-odd dice) for something that may ultimately result in nothing at all. So far, I have removed Initiative by having it rolled once, at the beginning, and then used throughout. <br /> I'm toying with the idea of removing the Soak step, and replacing it with a flat &quot;Soak Stamina+Armor damage&quot; rule, but that would obviously make the first few rounds null and void, and the later ones more lethal (Oblivional?).<br /> I may also rewrite Dodge into a single-die roll, with the difficulty being X-Dodge skill, but that messes with whatever balance was originally in the system.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fellow storytellers, do you have any ideas, suggestions, or comments on how to further reduce the amount of dice thrown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:25:47-07:00","id":486462,"title":"","content":"I recommend looking at how Aberrant revised the combat system. If I recall, soak was changed so that it always succeeded and needed no roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:28:37-07:00","id":486880,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">For combat, I used variants of First Edition (N)WoD. I kept Second Edition/Revised CWoD system for (most) everything else. I really liked the streamlined combat, which was usually resolved with one roll.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure how Second Edition NWoD handles things (or Aberrant Revised, to Octavo\u2019s point), but I agree \u2013 CWoD combat can bog down a session.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Disclaimer: I freely use and enjoy both systems and this post should not be taken as an instigation of Edition Warring. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T10:47:02-07:00","id":487432,"title":"","content":"At our table, the only combat step we roll for is &quot;to-hit.&quot; Initiative is Wits+Dexterity, damage is static - weapon type+attack successes, and soak is automatic. If another character is using their action to dodge, their roll subtracts from the attacker's &quot;to-hit&quot; successes.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T02:37:02-07:00","id":489194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/486446-streamlining-combat?p=487432#post487432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At our table, the only combat step we roll for is &quot;to-hit.&quot; Initiative is Wits+Dexterity, damage is static - weapon type+attack successes, and soak is automatic. If another character is using their action to dodge, their roll subtracts from the attacker's &quot;to-hit&quot; successes.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does this affect damage distribution? Making Soak automatic means that shooting a Wraith with stamina 5 with a pistol. Seems a bit odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5238,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","user":"Herbert_West","date":". 04-23-2015, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T10:24:05-07:00","id":489636,"title":"","content":"I assume you meant a light pistol, which has a listed Damage Rating of 4. That would be 4+attacker's &quot;to-hit&quot; successes, so the attacker would need to roll 3 or more successes to damage a character with a Stamina of 5. For a heavy pistol, the attacker would have to roll 2 or more. But if we can be honest for a moment, I'm not interested in the binomial distribution; I'm far more interested in mood, theme, and story. Streamlining combat to this point of efficiency has resulted in full rounds of four players plus NPC's lasting only a minute or two. Combat usually lasts three or four rounds, and the whole thing is resolved in less than ten minutes. If you'd like, I can lay out my whole revised combat script.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T12:58:46-07:00","id":489764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/486446-streamlining-combat?p=489636#post489636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you meant a light pistol, which has a listed Damage Rating of 4. That would be 4+attacker's &quot;to-hit&quot; successes, so the attacker would need to roll 3 or more successes to damage a character with a Stamina of 5. For a heavy pistol, the attacker would have to roll 2 or more. But if we can be honest for a moment, I'm not interested in the binomial distribution; I'm far more interested in mood, theme, and story. Streamlining combat to this point of efficiency has resulted in full rounds of four players plus NPC's lasting only a minute or two. Combat usually lasts three or four rounds, and the whole thing is resolved in less than ten minutes. If you'd like, I can lay out my whole revised combat script.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat would take forever in that case though. That means you have 5 points of automatic soak and the target has to get an outrageous amount of successes on the damage roll. You'd be sitting there for hours just waiting till the dice came up so damage could pierce through their soak. If you wore basic armor, like duct taping pillows to you, you'd basically be unstoppable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T13:22:27-07:00","id":489776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)the target has to get an outrageous amount of successes on the damage roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, actually. As provided in my example, an attacker needs to roll 3 or more successes while using a light pistol - the weakest listed firearm* - to injure a character with a Stamina rating of 5. Using a rifle or shotgun, both listed as 8 damage, an attacker only needs to roll a single success to cause 3 levels of Corpus damage to a wraith with 5 Stamina. Any successes rolled over the initial add to damage; rolling 5 successes to hit with a rifle causes 12 points of Corpus damage, subtracting the target's 5 Stamina still results in a total of 7 levels of damage to the target - more than half their Corpus lost in one attack!<br /> <br /> Let's be truthful here for a second: someone with 5 points of Stamina and 10 points of armor or whatever** isn't a character meant to be taken out by a lucky shot from a light pistol anyway. White-room scenarios are utter claptrap, and in other systems that utilize dice pool penalties from Health Levels, like <i>Vampire</i>, the wound penalties are applied to the automatic soak. <i>Wraith</i> doesn't follow the Health Level wound penalties idea; hence I didn't mention it.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> *Seriously, even the listed archaic firearms do 5 damage. And we're talking matchlocks and blunderbusses here.<br /> ** Good luck finding pillows on the other side of the Shroud.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 04-23-2015, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T15:35:13-07:00","id":489914,"title":"","content":"Nothing's suggestions work well. They're actually a very sensible set of suggestions for resolving combat quickly. One dice roll is nice and easy. I always skipped the initiative phase by having that be a static trait, and skipping the reverse-order declaration of actions phase.<br /> <br /> You could also use the WtGW skirmish rules to collapse multiple actions into one round of combat. This is only vaguely faster, but the rules can be tweaked again to speed things up a bit more.<br /> <br /> The simplest way is to just have everyone roll their relevant traits, compare the results, and have the ST abstract the rest. It's fast, but it will end up with some arguments if not handled consistently. I wouldn't do this unless the confrontation was something that absolutely needed to be glossed over or resolved quickly, but I do tend to use the extras rules for NPCs, so that they have fewer health levels and therefore drop out of play sooner. When battling spectres, I call for regular morale checks if the spectres take casualties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T02:58:57-07:00","id":490367,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I did not mean to imply that the suggestions would not work. In fact, they do work very well, even if the increased lethality meant I needed to wave my magic wand and cap the damage my player took.<br /> For some reason, they decided it would be a good idea to floor it when confronted with a roadblock and ten civil war era rifles pointed at them, instead of talking.....<br /> <br /> Point being: thank, they work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:15:38-07:00","id":490733,"title":"","content":"I think perhaps adambeyoncelowe was addressing theoutlander523's above post. I'm really glad the system works out for you though, and please, if you work out any tweaks or find something that runs a bit better one way than another, let me know. I'm always interested in refining these systems. And usually, whenever I present this idea, there are criticisms of &quot;increased lethality&quot; (like, seriously, it's the exact phrase everyone uses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), but I like to think of it more as &quot;consistent lethality.&quot; I mean, the book uses a system where it's possible to roll 10+ successes to hit, and then roll zilch for damage. Personally, I feel that even a chance of that happening is unfair (probably because it's happened to me once or twice).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:09:41-07:00","id":495111,"title":"","content":"Earlier I was flicking through the ST's Guide for Changeling again, and I remembered it had simplified combat rules. There were two sets of rules for this. I don't have my book with me now, but I'm going off memory.<br /> <br /> The first set of alternate rules reduces everything to one roll (after initiative), where players each state their intentions (disarm, injure, stun, wound, maim, kill, etc) and then roll to a varying difficulty (7 to disarm or injure, 8 to stun or wound, 9 to maim or kill). Three successes are required to achieve your desired result and modifiers might make this easier/harder. Injuring is 1-2 damage, wounding is 3-4, maiming incapacitates, while killing is self-explanatory. Two successes means a partial victory. One means a glancing blow. The ST decides the rest.<br /> <br /> The second set does away with dice altogether, and allows combatants to state their intentions and then compare stats. The ST gives modifiers based on good tactics, weapons and other combat advantages, and then applies it to the Attribute + Ability totals. No dice are rolled, but whoever has the higher score wins. The difference between their scores may indicate the degree of success.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}